  "summary": "devalue: Residual sparse-array CPU amplification in uneval",
  "details": "`uneval` performs synchronous work proportional to a sparse array's declared length. An application that passes attacker-influenced sparse values to `uneval` can suffer event-loop blocking. Since attacker-controlled creation of sparse arrays is so difficult, this vulnerability is very difficult to exploit.",
